{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1253445-1001-promethean-characters","id":1253445,"title":"1001 Promethean Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-11T18:29:28-07:00","id":1253445,"title":"1001 Promethean Characters","content":"Let's talk about interesting character ideas we've got in our heads! I'll start.<br /> <br /> Bob Birchwood, a Riven construct and nomadic, throngless practitioner of Aurum who works as an Amazon delivery man in order to avoid causing the Wasteland effect and still live among humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T21:44:14-07:00","id":1253487,"title":"","content":"In topics like this, you should add numbers to ideas - so in few dozen pages we would really hit 1001 ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Assuming yours were 1... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. <b>One of <a href=\"https://metro.co.uk/2017/09/13/looking-for-robot-love-here-are-5-sexbots-you-can-buy-right-now-6891378/\" target=\"_blank\">new sex robots</a> was used all here life just to satisfy one of her 'users'.</b> But the lonely man <i>truly </i>develop love for the machine, even if she did not say a word. And like Pygmalion in the myths, he breath life into her with a true love kiss. Now the once robot is (almost) real women with feelings. And her demiurge do not really know nuances of love...<br /> <br /> She would start on Aurum ( of course ) and I would go with making her a Galateid Construct, not Unfleshed, as those are two slightly different things. See quote below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p.76</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intent matters. Unfleshed are meant to be simulacra of humans, not humans themselves. They must be made of non-human parts, yes, but the creator must also desire something less than human: a robot, a living sculpture, an artificial intelligence, a puppet with a mind of its own. All of these things are alive, yes, but they were created with the expectation that they would not be human.<br /> Galatea was created to be the perfect human companion, so whether she was made from marble or not, she\u2019s not Unfleshed. Prometheans that aren \u2019t made from corpses are informally known as <b>constructs</b> and can be of any Lineage, depending on what their creator did to will them into existence. That brings up the question of humour: Would a Frankenstein made from machines and engines have Yellow Bile, as his progenitor, or Oil, as an artificial being? Either could be the case, but in the end it\u2019s up to you and what you<br /> want done with your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-12-2018, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T18:44:18-08:00","id":1365418,"title":"","content":"Topic necromancy by the passer-by fan of the <b>PtC</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Got idea on next character concept, but I'm not sure how to finalise it. Any help on those, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a>?<br /> <br /> 3. <i>Medieval Promethean</i> - called <b>'Pilgrim'</b> - like names points to, he travels around the world to go to sacred places, to prey for the sick on Contagions. Probably he would be Christian. But I'm blank on Linage and Refinement. Maybe Tammuz, to mark his 'creation from God'? ( Even if he would be Christian? Tammuz are Jewish Linage by tradition. ) I also have problem with pointing Refinement based on his Faith - Maybe Plumbum or Cuprum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T20:31:41-08:00","id":1365455,"title":"","content":"Medieval? Before there were Frankensteins (that is, any time before 1816, the Year Without a Summer \u2014 see Dark Eras Companion pp.204\u2013231), there were the Amirani \u2014 the Prophets (Dark Eras Companion pp.98\u201399). <br /> <br /> As for Refinements, there was a variant of Aurum called Pneuma, or Grace (Dark Eras Companion pp.164\u2013165). <br /> <br /> Personally, as a Christian, I find both the Lineage and the Refinement as written to be unnecessarily hostile to Christianity; and I use slightly modified versions of each that aren't as hostile. But that's just me. The point is that a Prophet pursuing the Refinement of Grace \u2014 in broad strokes at least \u2014 would be an excellent fit for your Pilgrim. Perhaps a little <i>too</i> excellent; you might want to deviate from one or the other just to avoid being too obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T13:58:59-08:00","id":1365603,"title":"","content":"I agree with Dataweaver's suggestion for Refinement. Assuming this is for your Werewolf game, obvious is probably the best way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1253445-1001-promethean-characters?p=1365418#post1365418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( Even if he would be Christian? Tammuz are Jewish Linage by tradition. )</div> </div> </div> </div>They're somewhat linked to the legends of golems but there's no necessary direct connection there. DAC somewhat implies that plenty of Tammuz are Christian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T21:59:48-07:00","id":1390704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1253445-1001-promethean-characters?p=1365455#post1365455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medieval? Before there were Frankensteins (that is, any time before 1816, the Year Without a Summer \u2014 see Dark Eras Companion pp.204\u2013231), there were the Amirani \u2014 the Prophets (Dark Eras Companion pp.98\u201399). <br /> <br /> As for Refinements, there was a variant of Aurum called Pneuma, or Grace (Dark Eras Companion pp.164\u2013165). <br /> <br /> Personally, as a Christian, I find both the Lineage and the Refinement as written to be unnecessarily hostile to Christianity; and I use slightly modified versions of each that aren't as hostile. But that's just me. The point is that a Prophet pursuing the Refinement of Grace \u2014 in broad strokes at least \u2014 would be an excellent fit for your Pilgrim. Perhaps a little <i>too</i> excellent; you might want to deviate from one or the other just to avoid being too obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I share your opinion on the matter regarding my faith, the Amirani do paint a rather negative and unflattering image as written.. but I dislike them more for the fact that they are just a lot less interesting than the Frankensteins are narratively to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway to add to these 1001 Created..<br /> <br /> 4. An Ulgan that walks the Path of Silver who has an adorable obsession with the other supernatural creatures in the world and is out to Catch, er, Catalog \u2018em all and discover how they can more or less coexist with humanity without the universe instinctually hating them. Think of him as sorta like Professor Oak if Prof. Oak was a dirty, slime covered Hobo.<br /> <br /> 5. A Zeka born from the Dropping of Little Boy, a creature made of ashes and bone who nonetheless is determined to discover a way to avenge those who died even decades later.. for surely whoever would scorch a population with the might of the Gods not once, but twice is a terrible force that deserves Nuclear retribution in return. Clearly a follower of Tin through and through\u2014 but seeking revenge is all too human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-22-2020, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:40:04-07:00","id":1390779,"title":"","content":"A couple more!<br /> <br /> 6. They call him Ikusa, though violence is the one thing this Unfleshed follower of Aurum is more averse to than any other. So he tries his best to help people resolve their problems as bloodlessly as possible either in person or online; a sort of cyberspace Advocate for the abused and dispossessed who, quite shamefully, can\u2019t seem to escape the more detestable portions of his original programming whenever Torment overtakes him.<br /> <br /> 7. There are urban legends of a beautiful monster who stalks the more decayed neighborhoods of Detroit called Mama Snags, a Muse fallen to the Path of Flux who\u2019s gained a reputation of snatching homeless children and teenagers up and literally eating them, using the remains to \u201cbirth\u201d a horrid little Family of her own. There is said to be an abandoned warehouse somewhere in town that serves as an art gallery-cum-nursery for her favorite creations: full of malformed, unmoving little monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T19:35:33-08:00","id":1421916,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s another!<br /> <br /> 8. Extempore are all unique, but the man who calls himself Groundhog is even more so: his birth was brought on by the interruption of a disaster that was sealed within a bubble of looped time, a mass shooting that would reoccur over and over again- all according to the designs of a mysterious clockwork god. The breaking of this loop caused a Firestorm to erupt at the location this massacre was meant to take place, and the only survivor out of the hundreds who were slaughtered would be a creature made of the myriad pieces of one individual who died thousands of times within the loop- a Matchless Created who is curiously able to come back to life endlessly provided that he meets his end through violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-04-2020, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}